# Register before call

Patients must be **registered on the website** before they can use Voia voice, chat, or phone calling.

## Rules

- Never allow anonymous web voice/chat sessions. Issue conversation tokens only for a verified registered session.
- Never connect inbound phone callers to the agent unless their caller ID matches a registered patient.
- Registration is phone-based (E.164 + SMS OTP). Do **not** require a full name.
- Care-data consent is collected at registration. Calling/chat is unlocked only after OTP verification.
- Unregistered phone callers get a short message directing them to register on the website first (and emergency guidance if needed).
- Appointment booking and care tools remain available only in the context of a registered patient where session checks apply.

## When changing related code

- Keep `/api/elevenlabs/token` session-gated.
- Keep `/api/webhooks/twilio/voice` registration-gated.
- Preserve the register → verify OTP → session cookie → call/chat flow in the UI.
